    "compose": "# Postgres plus a scheduled pg_dump sidecar. Both containers share the database\n# network; only the backup volume is mounted, and it is a named volume so the\n# dumps survive a `docker compose down`.\nname: arvion-postgres-backup\n\nservices:\n  postgres:\n    image: postgres:16.4-alpine\n    restart: unless-stopped\n    environment:\n      POSTGRES_DB: ${POSTGRES_DB:-app}\n      POSTGRES_USER: ${POSTGRES_USER:-app}\n      POSTGRES_PASSWORD: ${POSTGRES_PASSWORD:-change-me}\n    volumes:\n      - postgres-data:/var/lib/postgresql/data\n    healthcheck:\n      test: [\"CMD-SHELL\", \"pg_isready -U $${POSTGRES_USER} -d $${POSTGRES_DB}\"]\n      interval: 10s\n      timeout: 5s\n      retries: 5\n      start_period: 20s\n    mem_limit: 512m\n    cpus: 1.0\n    networks:\n      - database\n\n  backup:\n    image: prodrigestivill/postgres-backup-local:16-alpine\n    restart: unless-stopped\n    depends_on:\n      postgres:\n        condition: service_healthy\n    environment:\n      POSTGRES_HOST: postgres\n      POSTGRES_DB: ${POSTGRES_DB:-app}\n      POSTGRES_USER: ${POSTGRES_USER:-app}\n      POSTGRES_PASSWORD: ${POSTGRES_PASSWORD:-change-me}\n      SCHEDULE: \"@daily\"\n      BACKUP_KEEP_DAYS: ${BACKUP_KEEP_DAYS:-7}\n      BACKUP_KEEP_WEEKS: 4\n      HEALTHCHECK_PORT: 8080\n    volumes:\n      - backups:/backups\n    healthcheck:\n      test: [\"CMD\", \"wget\", \"-qO-\", \"http://localhost:8080/\"]\n      interval: 30s\n      timeout: 5s\n      retries: 3\n      start_period: 30s\n    mem_limit: 256m\n    cpus: 0.5\n    networks:\n      - database\n\nvolumes:\n  postgres-data:\n  backups:\n\nnetworks:\n  database:\n    driver: bridge\n",
    "envExample": "POSTGRES_DB=app\nPOSTGRES_USER=app\nPOSTGRES_PASSWORD=change-me\n# Number of daily dumps to keep before the oldest is removed.\nBACKUP_KEEP_DAYS=7\n",
    "readme": "# Postgres with backups\n\nPostgres 16 plus a sidecar that runs `pg_dump` on a schedule. The sidecar waits\nfor the database healthcheck before it starts, so the first dump is not empty.\n\n## Run\n\n```bash\ncp .env.example .env\ndocker compose up -d\ndocker compose logs -f backup        # shows the dump schedule\ndocker compose exec backup ls /backups\n```\n\n## Restore\n\nCopy a dump out, then restore into a scratch database:\n\n```bash\ndocker compose cp backup:/backups/last/app_latest.sql.gz ./app.sql.gz\ngunzip -c app.sql.gz | docker compose exec -T postgres psql -U app -d app\n```\n\n## Notes\n\n- The backup container is on the same private network; Postgres still publishes\n  no host port.\n- Dumps land in the named `backups` volume with daily, weekly and monthly\n  rotations handled by the image.\n- A backup you have never restored is not a backup. Run the restore above at\n  least once before trusting it.\n",
